# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git already stores mvnw with LF, but on Windows the default core.autocrlf=true checks it out with
# CRLF. The Docker build then copies that file into a Linux image, where the shebang reads
# "#!/bin/sh\r", the kernel looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the build dies
# with a bare "exit code: 127". Linux CI never reproduces it, because there the checkout is LF —
# so the production API image simply could not be built from a Windows checkout.
#
# Scoped deliberately: only files whose line endings actually change behaviour are pinned. A blanket
# "* text=auto" would renormalise the whole repository in one commit and bury real changes.

# Shell scripts and wrappers must stay LF — they are executed by a POSIX shell, including inside
# the Docker build stages.
mvnw            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
gradlew         text eol=lf

# The Windows wrapper is executed by cmd.exe and must stay CRLF.
mvnw.cmd        text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch, and never diff as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.jar           binary
